# Notes for coding agents

This is a [tifa](https://github.com/liustack/tifa) app. Go routes requests, loads data and runs the hooks. React pages render to HTML inside the Go process (QuickJS, no Node at run time), and TanStack Router takes over in the browser. The build makes one executable.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `{{.Install}}` | Install the npm packages (React, TanStack Router, TypeScript) |
| `go tool tifa dev` | Run at http://127.0.0.1:9527 and rebuild when the content of a Go, TypeScript, CSS or JSON file or `tifa.yaml` changes |
| `go tool tifa build` | Generate `.tifa/` and build `bin/` |
| `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` | Test and check the Go code |
| `{{.Run}} typecheck` | Check the TypeScript, once `tifa build` or `tifa dev` has written the types into `.tifa/` |
| `go tool tifa routes` | List the routes |

Never edit `.tifa/`. It is generated, and `go test ./...` skips it.

## Layout

- Code is grouped by domain, and a domain is a folder under `app/`. Its types, queries and rules sit next to its pages, with their tests. `app/todos/todo.go` (`package todos`) is the todo list. The home page (`app/route.go`) and the page of one todo (`app/todos/todo+/route.go`) import `{{.Module}}/app/todos`.
- A new domain gets a folder under `app/` and a file named after it, such as `app/notes/note.go` (`package notes`). When it has a list page and a page per item, its code goes in the list folder, not in the `name+` folder of one item.
- The root package (`package {{.Package}}`, at the module root) holds only the hooks (`hooks.go`) and what the whole app shares (`db.go`: `var DB`, and `schema.sql` with the tables of every domain). Domains import it as `"{{.Module}}"` and write `{{.Package}}.DB`. By convention it imports nothing under `app/`: Go refuses import cycles, so once a domain uses `{{.Package}}.DB`, the root package could not import that domain or a page that imports it.
- A domain may import another one that does not depend on it: if `notes` imports `todos`, directly or through other packages, `todos` cannot import `notes`. There are no `models/`, `services/` or `handlers/` packages. See [structure.md](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/structure.md).
- This app wires dependencies by hand: package-level variables such as `DB`, set up in `OnStart`, not in `init()`.

## Routes

- Every folder under `app/` is a URL segment. `app/` is `/`. `name+` is a parameter read with `c.Param("name")`. `name++` is the rest of the path, last folder only, `_splat` in TypeScript. Name the Go package after the parameter: `todo+` holds `package todo`.
- `route.go` holds `Load` (the page data) and the method handlers `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`. `route.tsx` is the page. A folder with `route.tsx` is a page, so it cannot define `GET`. A folder with only `route.go` is an API route and has no `Load`.
- `layout.go` (`func Layout`) and `layout.tsx` (with `<Outlet />`) wrap the page of their folder and every page below. `tifa.Use(c, pkg.Layout)` gets the data of an enclosing Layout, run once per request.
- Details: [app.md](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/app.md).

## Returned errors

| Returned | A page (`Load`, `Layout`) | A method handler |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `tifa.ErrNotFound`, or a `tifa.Error` with Status 404 | 404 with the first `NotFound` going up from the page (from the Layout one level up when a `Layout` returns it) | 404 as JSON |
| `tifa.Error{Status, Message}`, Status 400 to 599 but not 404 | That status, shown by the nearest `Error` | That status as JSON `{"error": message}` |
| `tifa.Fields{"field": "message"}` | 422, shown by the nearest `Error` | 422 as JSON with `"fields"` |
| `c.Redirect(url, code)` | A redirect | A redirect |
| Any other error, a panic, or a `tifa.Error` with another status | `OnError`, or a logged 500 without one | `OnError`, or a logged 500 without one |

`Validate` on a handler input runs before the handler. A `tifa.Error` or `tifa.Fields` it returns is answered as in the table. Any other error, also `tifa.ErrNotFound` or a `c.Redirect`, is answered with 400 and `err.Error()` as the message. A URL that matches no page shows the `NotFound` of the root `layout.tsx`, without the root Layout around it.

## Load and Ctx

The build reads `Load` and `Layout` and the functions they call to find which parameters each page depends on. It fails with the file and line when they:

- call `c.Param` or `c.Query` with a string that is not a constant, or not directly (stored in a variable or passed as a value),
- call `tifa.Use` with anything but a package-level `Layout` that wraps the caller,
- convert, store, return or send `c` anywhere else than a plain function or method of this module or of tifa, or a new local variable of the same type (see the docs for the full list),
- call `c.Request()` or `c.Writer()`.

Writing the response is checked when the request runs instead: in `Load` and `Layout`, `c.JSON`, `c.Text` and `c.NoContent` write nothing and return an error. Returned, that error is an unexpected one (`OnError`, or a 500). Setting headers and cookies is fine. Pass `c.Context()` when a function only needs the context. See [How Load may use Ctx](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/app.md#how-load-may-use-ctx).

## Handlers and the browser

- A typed handler takes an input after the Ctx, returns a result before the error, or both: `func POST(c *tifa.Ctx, in AddInput) (Todo, error)`. The framework decodes `in` from a JSON or form body (from the query string for `GET` and `DELETE`), runs `in.Validate()` if it exists, and writes the result as JSON (204 when there is no result). `func POST(c *tifa.Ctx) error` writes its own response.
- The data of `Load` and handler inputs and results travel as JSON, and tifa writes their TypeScript types. No interfaces, funcs or channels. A Go slice or map can be `null` in TypeScript, so write `?? []`.
- In TSX, import from the generated `./+route` of the folder: `route.useLoaderData()`, the `Data` type and one function per handler, such as `POST({ params, input })`. A Layout's data comes from `./+layout`. After a successful POST, PUT, PATCH or DELETE the page data loads again, unless the call passes `invalidate: false`.
- The function of a typed handler resolves to its result and throws `TifaError` (`status`, `message`, `fields`) for an error answer. The function of a handler that writes its own response resolves to the `Response`, also for a 4xx or 5xx, so check `response.ok`.
- A page may also export `head`, `NotFound` and `Error`. Components that need the browser at import time go in `*.client.tsx` and load with `clientOnly` from `tifa/client`.

## Hooks

`hooks.go` in the root package, all optional:

- `OnStart()` runs before the app listens. An error stops the app.
- `OnShutdown(ctx)` runs after a stop signal, once the requests in flight have finished. Requests still running after `server.shutdown_timeout` are canceled and get one more `shutdown_timeout` to return. `OnShutdown` is skipped if they do not, and either way the app exits with status 1.
- `OnRequest(c)` runs before pages, navigation data requests, API routes and unmatched URLs, not static files. Call `c.Next()` to go on.
- `OnError(c, err)` gets unexpected errors and panics. Writing one replaces the default, which logs and answers 500.

## Tests

- Domain code: plain Go tests next to it, such as `app/todos/todo_test.go`. Each test gets a fresh database with `useTestDB(t)`, which replaces `{{.Package}}.DB`, so these tests do not run in parallel.
- Route code: `tifatest.NewCtx(t, httptest.NewRequest(...))` gives a `*tifa.Ctx`. Set path parameters with `r.SetPathValue`. Run `Load` and `Layout` through `tifa.Use(c, Load)`, call handlers directly, and test `Validate` on its own. These tests check what the function returns, not the HTTP answer. See [Testing](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/app.md#testing).

## Settings and data

- `tifa.yaml` lists every setting commented out at its default, with an example for `ssr.vms`, whose default is GOMAXPROCS. See [config.md](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/config.md). Environment variables starting with `TIFA_` are settings, and an unknown one stops the app, so do not use that prefix for your own.
- The database is `app.db` (or `$DB_PATH`). `schema.sql` runs at every start, so keep its statements safe to repeat (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`). A new domain adds its tables there. `tifa dev` does not watch `schema.sql`: after changing it, restart `tifa dev`.
- Build and generated files: [build.md](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/build.md). `tifa dev`: [dev.md](https://github.com/liustack/tifa/blob/main/docs/dev.md).
